WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:02.701
-Our next guests
are the writers and producers

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:03.968
behind the movie "Dumb Money,"

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:05.300
which is playing
in theaters now.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.534
Let's take a look.

00:00:06.534 --> 00:00:08.567
-Hey, do you -- do you remember
back at Stonehill

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:11.000
when they dared me
to run that mile naked?

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.634
-Yeah, there was a crazy storm
that night.

00:00:12.634 --> 00:00:14.267
-Everybody remembers that.
-Okay.

00:00:14.267 --> 00:00:15.934
-They do, man.
You don't think people remember

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.267
your four-minute,
three-second mile?

00:00:17.267 --> 00:00:20.467
-Oh, what is this, a pep talk?
-Stop hiding.

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:21.901
Seriously, okay?

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:24.734
Stop being all meek and [bleep]
and running away.

00:00:24.734 --> 00:00:26.234
-What, you want me to run
through lightning

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.133
with my [bleep] out?
-Yeah.

00:00:28.133 --> 00:00:30.968
Please. Exactly that.

00:00:30.968 --> 00:00:32.400
Run through lightning
with your [bleep] out.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:34.000
[Bleep] it.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:36.334
-Please welcome to the show
Lauren Schuker Blum

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:38.501
and Rebecca Angelo, everybody!

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:40.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:49.033
♪♪

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:57.601
♪♪

00:00:57.601 --> 00:00:59.534
Welcome! I'm so happy
to have you both here.

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:00.901
-We're happy to be here.

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.667
-And, you know, we don't often
have two guests at once,

00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.567
but you are the best
coordinated outfits

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.300
I've ever seen on the show.
-We tried.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.334
-You tried very hard,
and it paid off big time.

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:11.133
-She's in charge of outfits.
I just listen.

00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.200
-Yeah.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.234
-So, I think
the GameStop phenomenon

00:01:15.234 --> 00:01:16.868
was something
we were all aware of,

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:19.601
but maybe didn't fully
understand the details of.

00:01:19.601 --> 00:01:21.868
For those who weren't fully
up to speed on it,

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:24.834
can you just explain what
happened in that moment at time?

00:01:24.834 --> 00:01:26.834
-Yeah, it's David and Goliath.

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:31.067
It is the insane, true story
of thousands of regular people

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:34.067
who came together and beat
Wall Street at its own game.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.901
-And they were led
by this guy Keith Gill,

00:01:36.901 --> 00:01:38.467
who went by the name
Roaring Kitty

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.133
and Deep [bleep] Value online.

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:41.534
He had two names.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:44.868
And he is...you know,
he's funny, he's weird.

00:01:44.868 --> 00:01:49.000
He did his YouTube videos in cat
T-shirts with a red headband.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.200
And he made fifty --
almost $50 million overnight

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.834
from GameStop, that
video game store at the mall

00:01:54.834 --> 00:01:57.501
that we went to
as nerdy eight-year-olds.

00:01:57.501 --> 00:01:58.934
-So, the thing about GameStop is

00:01:58.934 --> 00:02:01.434
hedge funds
had shorted the company,

00:02:01.434 --> 00:02:03.701
which meant that
if the business failed

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.834
and everybody who worked there
lost their jobs,

00:02:05.834 --> 00:02:08.501
the hedge fund guys
would get rich.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.334
But Keith and thousands
or even millions of other people

00:02:11.334 --> 00:02:14.334
bought into the stock,
which sent the price soaring.

00:02:14.334 --> 00:02:16.167
A bunch of them
got rich in the process,

00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:18.467
and a few hedge funds
went under.

00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:20.300
-And dumb money,
I did not realize,

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:23.100
is an actual term
that Wall Street uses

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:25.267
about the kind of investor
that Keith was.

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.734
-Right. Well, Wall Street
calls itself smart money.

00:02:27.734 --> 00:02:29.534
Real, you know, original.

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.334
And they call retail investors
dumb money.

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:35.033
-So, in the moment
where the dumb money

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.367
was buying up GameStop,

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.868
they did not take it
seriously at first,

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:40.601
because they thought this just
proved their actual thesis,

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:43.601
which is that if we're on
the right side of this deal,

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:44.934
that has to be...
-Exactly.

00:02:44.934 --> 00:02:46.701
The whole story
caught everyone by surprise.

00:02:46.701 --> 00:02:48.767
-Yeah, they call it --
they call it a herding event.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.100
So, like, literally they view
regular people as cattle.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:55.501
So, did not take it seriously
until it was way too late.

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:58.033
-You guys met writing
for the Wall Street Journal.

00:02:58.033 --> 00:03:00.701
And how, when you write
a screenplay like this,

00:03:00.701 --> 00:03:02.534
how does your background
as reporters help

00:03:02.534 --> 00:03:04.267
in, you know,
putting this story together?

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:06.767
-It's so helpful. I think
we're still reporters at heart,

00:03:06.767 --> 00:03:09.334
and we interviewed
so many people on Wall Street,

00:03:09.334 --> 00:03:10.767
we talked to retail traders,

00:03:10.767 --> 00:03:13.868
and pretty much everything
in the movie is true,

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.601
except for one thing.

00:03:15.601 --> 00:03:17.467
Pete Davidson,
who stars in the film,

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.901
plays a real guy
named Kevin Gill,

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.567
and Kevin is a DoorDasher.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.567
He's an excellent DoorDasher
with a --

00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:24.968
-The real Kevin is an excellent
DoorDasher.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.801
He has a 99% rating.
-Okay.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:28.167
-But when we cast
Pete Davidson,

00:03:28.167 --> 00:03:30.501
we realized we can't sell
Pete Davidson

00:03:30.501 --> 00:03:33.000
as an excellent DoorDasher.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.167
So we made him a DoorDasher
from hell in the movie.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:37.501
-Gotcha.
-He eats people's food,

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.234
he drinks their drinks.

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:42.000
He's driving his car
all over their lawns.

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.667
-Now, you guys have been
up against something

00:03:44.667 --> 00:03:45.901
that a lot of films
have been up about.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.734
You have this incredible cast --

00:03:47.734 --> 00:03:51.167
Paul Dano, Nick Offerman,
Seth Rogen...

00:03:51.167 --> 00:03:53.167
-Sebastian Stan.
-America Ferrera.

00:03:53.167 --> 00:03:54.501
-It's a great cast,

00:03:54.501 --> 00:03:56.667
but unfortunately,
no one is able to go out

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:58.200
because of the SAG strike
and do press.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:00.067
Which means that
as writers and producers,

00:04:00.067 --> 00:04:03.067
you have been doing a great deal
of press for this movie.

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:05.200
Has that been
a strange experience?

00:04:05.200 --> 00:04:07.000
-Yes. [ Laughs ]

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.067
-Yeah. I wouldn't say...

00:04:09.067 --> 00:04:11.701
We're, like, not supposed to be
brought into direct sunlight.

00:04:11.701 --> 00:04:13.767
We're supposed to be
kept in, like, a closet.

00:04:13.767 --> 00:04:16.167
-Yeah, writers are, like, behind
their laptops, hunched over.

00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:18.834
And here we are
on national television.

00:04:18.834 --> 00:04:20.701
You know, we were at
the Toronto Film Festival.

00:04:20.701 --> 00:04:23.667
We pulled up to the red carpet
in our car

00:04:23.667 --> 00:04:25.200
and we could hear
the crowd going crazy.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.534
They were like,
"Yes, it's Seth Rogen!"

00:04:26.534 --> 00:04:28.701
And then the doors open,
and the crowd was like, "Oh."

00:04:28.701 --> 00:04:30.534
They got us.

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.367
-You did take a lovely photo
on the red carpet.

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:33.434
Like, don't
sell yourself short.

00:04:33.434 --> 00:04:35.100
-We're trying so hard.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.067
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.067 --> 00:04:40.367
-Those bags, our friend

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:42.467
who designs Edie Parker
made those for us.

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:44.834
And they say "dumb" on one side
and "money" on the other.

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:47.267
And we got out of our car
so confidently

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.968
and held up our bags and
were smiling for the cameras.

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:53.567
And then somebody ran up to us
and switched around Lauren's bag

00:04:53.567 --> 00:04:55.067
because she was flashing "dumb."

00:04:55.067 --> 00:04:56.467
So, we were like idiots,

00:04:56.467 --> 00:04:58.200
just like smiling
for the camera,

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:00.901
And it just said, "Dumb dumb."

00:05:00.901 --> 00:05:03.000
-You're like, "We're famous!
Dumb dumb!"

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.834
-Yes.

00:05:04.834 --> 00:05:07.834
-Your husband, Jason Blum,
who's a film producer,

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.300
he was actually here last week.
-He was.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.667
-And he was talking
about the fact

00:05:10.667 --> 00:05:12.000
that he had a movie
coming out,

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.400
and then he had
to change the date

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.334
because Taylor Swift
had a movie coming out.

00:05:15.334 --> 00:05:17.467
He didn't want to open
the same weekend as her.

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:19.100
-Right.
-But then the issue was

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.601
that he might have
to move to the weekend

00:05:20.601 --> 00:05:22.767
your movie was coming out,
and he said that was very tense.

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:24.067
-Yeah. Jerk.
-Yeah.

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.000
-Yeah, he stole our weekend.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:27.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:27.167 --> 00:05:28.868
-So, ultimately,
did it all work out okay?

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.534
-Things are going okay, yes.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.701
But he had a competing project
to ours, also.

00:05:32.701 --> 00:05:34.067
-Yeah.
-His own...

00:05:34.067 --> 00:05:36.200
-Oh, he had his own...
-He had his own GameStop movie.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.067
So we had a kind of, like,
Cold War in our house.

00:05:39.067 --> 00:05:41.067
And every time the studio
called with notes,

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:44.400
I had to, like, hide
in the closet to take the notes.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.801
And then I would open
the door afterwards

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.501
and I would hit Jason
in the face

00:05:47.501 --> 00:05:49.801
'cause he was waiting outside,
eavesdropping.

00:05:49.801 --> 00:05:51.801
-How could he do that
to his own wife?

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.000
-And our children were like
spies somehow, you know.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:55.667
It was a tough 18 months.
-Alright.

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:57.534
I'm glad that you came out
the winner

00:05:57.534 --> 00:05:59.200
on the GameStop saga.
-The important thing is we won.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:00.434
-Yes, you did win.

00:06:00.434 --> 00:06:01.934
And it's really
a wonderful movie,

00:06:01.934 --> 00:06:03.300
and I hope that people
go out and see it.

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:04.801
I enjoyed it a great deal,
and it's so lovely

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.467
to have you both here.
Thank you so much.

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:10.133
You guys,
that's Lauren Schuker Blum

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:11.634
and Rebecca Angelo, everybody.

00:06:11.634 --> 00:06:13.100
"Dumb Money"
is in theaters now.

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.467
Be right back
with more "Late Night."

